bilities that perfectly complement  those of their team partners  combined this results in a pretty  battle-hardened squad that won't back  down from  any challenge star wars bad badge is  scheduled for release  on may 4th on disney plus so you'll be  able to watch it soon  also of course marvel is fairly present  in disney's announcement so among other  releases  falcon and the winter soldier will  arrive on march 19th  as well as loki on june 11th another  highlight is the series sequel to the  popular animated thumb monsters  inc called monsters at work on july 2nd  on march 4th the previous streaming  service cbs all  access will be replaced by paramount  plus included are of course the major  cinema films but in contrast to walnut  brothers counterpart hbo max paramount  is pursuing a different strategy  movies are not to appear on the same day  but 30 to 45 days  after their actual release included are  titles such as a quiet place 2 and  mission impossible 7.  another special feature is a deal  between mgm  and paramount that for instance includes  the release of the new bond film  no time to die also featured is the new  star trek series strange new worlds and  fans of the halo franchise can soon  expect a series based on the games  as well paramount parent company viacom  cbs also owns networks such as showtime  nickelodeon and comedy central so you  can look forward to both familia  and new content here too since the end  of 2014 work has already been underway  on the new dc film  the flash many years followed without  significant progress and especially some  unsuccessful staff decisions a few days  ago  producer barbara muschietti finally  uploaded the first set picture of a  large warehouse with her husband  it director andy muschietti in the  foreground  shortly after the next piece of positive  news came out  as they finally found an actress for the  new supergirl  namely sasha cal she will thereby  supersede melissa benoist who played  supergirl in the flash series for six  seasons the long-awaited reboot of the  dc superhero universe is finally getting  the ball rolling as the flash is  supposed to be the kickoff for the  multiverse concept  similar to that of the mcu along with  this comes an appearance by both  michael keaton and ben affleck who will  stand in front of the camera together as  the batman  currently there is also rumor that danny  devito will take on the role of oswald  cobblepot aka  penguin we are eagerly awaiting further  cast editions and the apparent  approaching shooting start  and we're looking forward to the release  of the flash on november 4th  2022 to the excitement of many fans it  was announced a few days ago that the  original creators of the avatar animated  series  will soon be producing new content  avatar studios has been created together  with nickelodeon and has a tweet from  nickelodeon indicates  several adventures around the  protagonist and a plan for the future  an official press release states that  several series and movies based on the  world of avatar the last airbender and  the legend of korra  are being planned as well up front are  the avatar creators and producers  michael dimartino and brian konietzko  it has not yet been revealed what role  the comics which have been expanding the  avatar verse for quite some time will  play in this  at the same time the live action  adaption is still  in the works at netflix the martino and  kaniesco dropped out of the project some  time ago however  and there are probably only a few fans  who are seriously looking forward to it  in any case  we are excited to see which kind of  projects avatar studios will tackle  and we'll keep you up to date as usual  things are going pretty well for tom  holland at the moment the third  spiderman movie is coming out soon he's  also starring in the upcoming uncharted  and in addition to all the a-list movies  he can also play more serious roles for  example in  cherry and the devil all the time but  obviously it didn't just come to him  because as the 24 year old recently  revealed in an interview with backstage  he even auditioned for a role in  disney's star wars trilogy  if a rather funny mishap hadn't happened  to him back then we would probably see  tom holland in the role of the  stormtrooper and later resistance  fighter  finn today he's said to have mastered  the first casting rounds  brilliantly but when he then auditioned  for a scene with a woman who made droid  noises he just couldn't keep himself  from laughing  needless to say he didn't get the part  and john boyega  beat out the others do you think tom  holland would have fit the role of finn  as well as boyega or do you think it's a  good thing that he didn't get the role  in the end  feel free to let us know your opinion in  the comments  [Music]  huh

